21
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.064
This agent is going to be searching for healthcare providers

22
00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.765
using a specific MCP tool.

23
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.168
I'll load in a JSON file that

24
00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.236
I have stored in the data directory.

25
00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.039
And I'll load it in as a list called doctors.

26
00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.842
Then I'll use the MCP tool

27
00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.044
decorator to make this next method we're

28
00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.146
going to create into an MCP tool.

29
00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.449
This method is called list_doctors.

30
00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.350
So I'll have it take in

31
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.352
a US state name and a city.

32
00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.955
And it'll return a list of dictionaries.

33
00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:32.058
And remember to put in a detailed docstring,

34
00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.761
because this will be used by the LLM

35
00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.163
to decide which functions to call and when.

36
00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.402
This method will first do some input validation

37
00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.105
to make sure at least a city or a state is provided.

38
00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:49.175
We'll normalize the city and state to do case-insensitive matching.

39
00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.879
So now, we'll filter down the list by state and city.

40
00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.181
using a list comprehension.

41
00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.685
FastMCP will automatically convert this list of dictionaries

42
00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.687
into JSON when sending to the model.

43
00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.989
Now, I'll kick off the server with dunder main

44
00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.391
and run the MCP server over standard IO.

45
00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.994
This means the server will be running locally.

46
00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.763
Now that you have the MCP server set up,

